- WG | keep the job and the family evenings, and let it be a fine thing made | self_control: - | v: security, benevolence | tribal: keep to the hunt and the hearth, and let it be a fine thing made | magic: keep the master's work and the household's evenings, and let it be a fine thing made | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 75
- WU | write it up for the engineers' journal, with every measurement checked twice | grants: name in the field | v: achievement, conformity | tribal: tell the making of it at the gathering's fire, every step in its right order | magic: write it up for the artificers' guild book, with every measure checked twice | chance: 75
works: Within the year the first ones have gone to people who paid for them, and {N} is an inventor, with a living to make from it.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the thing on the bench goes out into the world in some form, and {N} is proud of the road taken.
fails: The first buyers are slow, the money runs out before the orders come, and {N} goes back to the trade with the model on a shelf.
fails: A rival with deeper pockets brings out something very like it, and {Ns} version is lost in the crowd.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6. an invention in every home (pairs D2b)
# The summit door: an inventor of four years or more whose invention has a following (LIFE_CALLINGS gate). Every
# colour's way of getting it into every home takes the facet [celebrated inventor] at the real chance, 6, with [an
# invention in everyday use]: a step at real odds, not a long shot, so no perk on failure. The pairs, at 75, are the
# honest other ways: the design given away, a licence for a share of every one sold, an apprentice taught the whole of
# it, investors and a board with honest books, faith kept with the small makers who took it on first. Every colour's
# mean is 40.5.

== an invention in every home
tier: life event
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-100
holds: inventor
tenure: 4-100
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .03 .02
drivers: era+.3 prosper+.2
times: per inventor of four years or more a year: about 1 in 40 has a real chance to get an invention into ordinary homes everywhere; most never do, and about 5 lives in 100,000 become inventors whose invention most households know (catalogue share; estimate)
likelier: good years when people buy new things, a patent held, a big maker looking for something new, a name in the field
rarer: hard years, a rival's copy already in the shops, no money for the tooling, an invention only specialists need
gap: 4-10
domain: career.5
tone: joy
life: work, money, publiclife
horizon: years
roles: boss, rival, partner, colleague, friend
earth: the invention sells, the big makers ring, and it could be in every home in the land, or in hardly any
tribal: other bands want the new tool, and it could become a tool every band makes, or be forgotten in a few winters
magic: the device sells at the fairs, the great houses send their stewards, and it could stand in every household of the realm
scene: Four years after the first one sold, {Ns} invention has a following: a few thousand in use, letters from strangers, a shop in the city that sells out every month. Now a big maker wants to talk, a morning show wants a demonstration, and {rival}'s cheaper copy has turned up on a market stall. This is the year it goes into every home, or goes back to being a good idea a few people liked.
scene W: Every home means every safety standard, every shop's buyer and every rule about what may go on a shelf. {N} has the forms spread out on the kitchen table.
scene U: At the price it costs now, only the keen buy it. {N} keeps coming back to one question: how to make it so simple and so cheap that anyone would.
scene B: The big maker has shops on every high street. One signature on the right terms, and {Ns} name goes into all of them; on the wrong terms, the name goes nowhere.
scene R: {N} would rather show it to people than talk about it: in town squares, at fairs, on the morning show, wherever there is a crowd.
scene G: The letters are the best part: a farmer, a nurse, an old man who can open his own jars again. {N} wants it to reach people like them, and to go on reaching them.
scene tribal: Traders from three bands have asked for {Ns} new tool this summer, and at the gathering a far band's toolmaker was already making a poor copy. Made well and shown widely, it could become a tool every band makes; if not, it will be forgotten in a few winters.
scene magic: The device sells out at every fair, the great houses send their stewards with contracts, and a rival workshop's cheap copy has appeared in the market. {N} can see it standing in every household of the realm, or fading into a curiosity in a few cabinets.
