- URG | build a second, better one just for the joy of it, and keep it at home | grants: prototyping | v: self-direction, hedonism | tribal: make a second, better one just for the joy of it, and keep it at your own hearth | magic: build a second, better one just for the joy of it, and keep it for the household | foot: place prod.craft | chance: 83
- BRG | sell the first few at the weekend market, and see who comes back for more | v: stimulation, power | tribal: trade the first few at the gathering, and see who comes back for more | magic: sell the first few at the weekend market in the square, and see who comes back for more | foot: place comm.market | chance: 83
works: A year later strangers are paying for it, a maker has taken it on, and {N} gives up the old work to be an inventor, with a bench and a list of orders.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the thing made for fun turns out to be a good beginning, and {N} is still making things a year on.
fails: The interest fades as fast as it came, and the thing goes back to being a toy for the household.
fails: The answers are polite and few, and {N} puts the drawings in a drawer, where they stay for years.

# ================================================================ world-only

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9. the guild commissions a flying ship (only: magic; pairs D6b)
# The artificers' guild wants a ship that flies (callings/worlds.py, WORLD_ONLY_CALLINGS), for an inventor of three
# years or a civil engineer or machinist of six (LIFE_CALLINGS gate; `tenure: 3-99` here). The singles are each for one
# rung, as the art pack's 'the manuscript in the pile on the floor' (option requires: names one title, so each single
# carries `requires: <its rung> | without: impossible` and is never offered to anyone it does not fit): Blue's and
# Black's are the inventor's try for the facet [celebrated inventor] (the realm's artificer) at its real chance, 6;
# White's is the civil engineer's and Red's and Green's the machinist's try for [inventor] (an artificer) at 25. The
# inventor sees two singles, the civil engineer one and the machinist two; every colour still has its answer in the
# pairs, which everyone the gate lets in meets. The enchanter's binding that makes the hull rise sits on the pair UB
# (Blue's knowledge of what a binding does, Black's purse): someone else's magic, bought (requires savings; a loan
# otherwise, lacking .5), never the artificer's own gift, with the Order's disapproval on a closed: approval line and
# its price in the backfire; it gives the talk of the guild ([name in the field]), not the title, which the guild gives
# only for a ship of the artificer's own making. The other pairs, at 55, are the honest ways: a kite-ship for the fair,
# the hill-folk's kite-makers, the old artificer put forward, a year for a small model first. The binding, at 93, is
# solved around the two singles at 6 until every colour's mean is 40.

== the guild commissions a flying ship
tier: life event
only: magic
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-100
holds: inventor | civil engineer | machinist
tenure: 3-99
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .02 .01
times: per artificer of three years, or engineer or machinist of the guild of six, in the magic world a year: about 1 in 50 hears that the artificers' guild wants a ship that flies and will choose who builds it (estimate); a ship that keeps the air is the realm's newest wonder, and few artificers in a generation build one
likelier: a guild flush with the court's silver, a name for clever work, a flood or a famine that needs fast carrying, an old artificer retiring
rarer: lean years, a guild master with a favourite, an Order that frowns on new wonders, a workshop far from the capital
gap: 5-10
domain: career.5
tone: joy
life: work, publiclife
horizon: years
roles: boss, rival, mentor, colleague
magic: the artificers' guild wants a ship that flies, and will choose who builds it
scene magic: The guild master reads the commission aloud in the long hall: the court wants a ship that flies, to carry the realm's letters over the mountains in a day, and the guild will choose who builds it. A model of a hull hangs from the rafters, and nobody has yet made one keep the air. In the lanes behind the guildhall an enchanter sells bindings that make a thing rise, for a price, and without the Order's leave.
scene magic W: The guild has a code for every beam and rivet, learned the hard way over two hundred years of fallen bridges. {N} means to build a ship that keeps every line of it.
scene magic U: Nobody knows yet why a bird stays up. {N} has watched gulls over the harbour for a month with a notebook, and suspects it is not the flapping at all.
scene magic B: Whoever builds this ship will be the realm's artificer, with a hall of their own and the court's ear. {rival} has already been seen dining with the guild master, and {N} has heard about the enchanter's bindings.
scene magic R: {N} wants to be the first one up there: over the rooftops, over the river, with the wind in the rigging and the whole city looking up.
scene magic G: The hill-folk have flown great kites over the high pastures for longer than the guild has existed. {N} wonders whether anyone in the long hall has ever thought to ask them.
- W | draw the ship to the guild's every rule, and prove each beam on paper first | title: inventor | requires: civil engineer | without: impossible | v: conformity, security | chance: 25
- U | work out from first principles how wings and wind could carry a hull | title: celebrated inventor | requires: inventor | without: impossible | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 6
- B | promise the guild a ship by midsummer, and hire the best hands in the city | title: celebrated inventor | requires: inventor | without: impossible | binds | v: power, achievement | chance: 6
- R | build a small ship in the yard with your own hands, and fly it yourself | title: inventor | requires: machinist | without: impossible | body: light | v: stimulation | chance: 25
- G | build it light, the way the birds and the old kite-makers of the hills do | title: inventor | requires: machinist | without: impossible | v: tradition, universalism | chance: 25
- BR | build a kite-ship for the midsummer fair, and charge for the first rides | v: stimulation, power | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 55
- RG | go up to the hill-folk's kite-makers, and learn how their great kites ride the wind | grants: mentor | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 55
- UB | buy an enchanter's binding that makes the hull rise, without the Order's leave | grants: name in the field | requires: savings | without: means | lacking: .5 | mark: defied an authority | closed: approval: an enchanter's binding bought without the Order's leave; backfire: the binding fades with the year, and the enchanter's price to renew it rises each time | self_control: - | v: power, achievement | chance: 93
- WG | put the old artificer forward, who has waited all their life for this | mark: helped someone in need | v: benevolence, universalism | chance: 55
- WU | ask the guild for a year to build and test a small model first | grants: prototyping | binds | v: security, achievement | foot: place prod.craft | chance: 55
works: On a still morning in late summer the ship lifts off the guild's field, turns once over the river, and the whole city comes out onto the roofs to watch.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the guild remembers the year of the flying ship, and {Ns} part in it.
fails: The ship rises a few feet, lurches, and settles back onto the field, and the guild gives the commission to {rival}.
fails: The court's silver runs out before the hull is finished, and the commission is put away for a better year.
